## Regression test: llvm-bolt -debug must not crash when dumping
## instructions that carry MCPlus annotations.
##
## BOLT appends a null Inst-kind marker operand to every annotated
## instruction (MCPlusBuilder::setAnnotationOpValue). MCOperand::print
## dereferenced the marker operand unconditionally, so any
## LLVM_DEBUG(MCInst::dump()) of an annotated instruction crashed with
## SIGSEGV. The jump table in this test drives the indirect-branch
## analysis (computeLocalUDChain) which dumps annotated instructions,
## reproducing the crash: llvm-bolt used to die during disassembly and
## now completes. Found with -rewrite -debug on redis-server; the same
## guard protects the raw dump() sites in ShrinkWrapping, AllocCombiner
## and FrameOptimizer.

# REQUIRES: system-linux

# RUN: %clang %cflags -O2 -Wl,-q -fuse-ld=lld -nostartfiles -e _start \
# RUN:   %S/Inputs/debug-inst-dump.c -o %t.orig
# RUN: llvm-bolt %t.orig -o /dev/null -rewrite -debug 2>/dev/null
